	(text_box "Like the IBM PC, the Chameleon stores even parity bits in the 9th DRAM chip (bit D8)\n\nWhen writing, the parity bit input to the parity generator is forced to 0. The even parity result calculated from bits 0-7 is driven to data bit 8 to be stored.\n\nWhen reading, the parity bit D8 is included in the parity calculation, flipping the result of the calculation to odd parity. \n\nThus, an asserted EVEN_PARITY signal during a read operation may be considered a parity error.\n\n\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.11 336.55 0)
		(size 63.5 27.94)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
